STUDENT OUTCOMES (SO) 

After the completion of the program, the graduates of the BSIT program 
shall be able to: 

a. apply the knowledge of computing, science, and mathematics 
appropriate to the discipline; 
b. understand best practices and standards and their applications; 
c. analyze complex problems, identify and define the computing 
requirements appropriate to its solution; 
d. identify and analyze user needs and take them into account in the 
selection, creation, evaluation, and administration of computer -based 
system; 
e. design, implement and evaluate computer -based systems, processes, 
components, or programs to meet desired needs and requirements under 
various constraints; 
f. integrate IT-based solutions into the under environment effectively;
